---
// Giscus comments via GitHub Discussions.
//
// There were no existing comment threads at migration, so comments move to the
// new repo with simple `pathname` mapping (one thread per post URL, /posts/{slug})
// — no legacy-term continuity needed, and the old blog repo can be fully retired.
//
// SET BEFORE CUTOVER: giscus needs a PUBLIC repo with Discussions enabled + the
// giscus GitHub App installed. Point data-repo at it and paste the two IDs from
// https://giscus.app (data-repo-id, data-category-id).
---

<section class="comments" aria-label="Comments">
  <h2 id="comments">Comments</h2>
  <script
    is:inline
    src="https://giscus.app/client.js"
    data-repo="digital-grease/apps.digitalgrease.github.io"
    data-repo-id="R_kgDOSKEXLQ"
    data-category="Announcements"
    data-category-id="DIC_kwDOSKEXLc4C_CgY"
    data-mapping="pathname"
    data-strict="1"
    data-reactions-enabled="1"
    data-emit-metadata="0"
    data-input-position="top"
    data-theme="dark_dimmed"
    data-lang="en"
    crossorigin="anonymous"
    async></script>
</section>

<style>
  .comments {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .comments h2 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
</style>
